 "intro": {
  "title": "THE UNRUNG GATE",
  "lines": [
   "A short walk, in silence.",
   "At the Gate: light the lamp (L), and keep it lit."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The door is a door again. Behind you the stair is lit all the way down, and in front of you the lamp is steady.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "floor",
   "at": [13, 13],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The floor of the Bell. The roots have drawn back from the walls and left the stone clean, as if it had been waiting for someone to sweep it."
  },
  {
   "id": "shaft",
   "at": [31, 13],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The stair goes up the inside of the shaft. A plate at the first landing says how far down this is. I do not read the number."
  },
  {
   "id": "hive",
   "at": [49, 13],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The Hive, and nothing moving in it. The organs hang where they hung and none of them swells. Whatever kept the beat has stopped."
  },
  {
   "id": "deep",
   "at": [67, 13],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The city under the stone. Every lamp out, and one bell, high up, that nobody is ringing. It sways a little. I count three swings and then I stop counting."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [67, 16],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "One stretch of the south wall sounds different under my knuckles. Somebody has been here with a hand and a reason."
  },
  {
   "id": "steppe",
   "at": [85, 13],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A road across a plain under a low red sun. It is not the one I walked. It is the one that was always going to be here when I got to this end."
  },
  {
   "id": "gate",
   "at": [103, 13],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "Ines. I have you on the set. There is no line down there, and I have you. What is in front of you?"
  },
  {
   "id": "door",
   "at": [106, 13],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A door that is also a bell. A hook beside it, the kind a lamp hangs from. My father said what a lamp is for. Light it, and keep it lit."
  },
  {
   "id": "lit",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "The bell on the door has gone quiet. It is holding."
  },
  {
   "id": "page",
   "at": [67, 19],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 16, later. ringing, once in a very long while. I have timed it against my pulse, and my pulse is slower than it was. It is not the water. Whoever finds this: not the water."
  }
 ],
